WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Claude code now works with iMessage and

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:06.120
is changing the AI space forever. No

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.520
laptop, no VS code, no terminal. All I

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:10.320
need is a single iPhone that I use to

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:11.600
tell Claude code to do whatever I want

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.080
it to do. In this video, I'm going to

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.040
show you exactly how to set up Claude

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:17.080
code's new iMessage channel, how I use

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:18.760
it to run my AI agency while I'm away

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:21.080
from my desk, [music] and how you can

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:23.120
use it to build and scale a powerful

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:24.640
one-person AI business. So, here's the

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:26.160
thing. If you're running any kind of AI

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.960
business, whether it's an agency,

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.680
building apps, freelancing, whatever it

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.280
is, you know the pain of being tied to

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:33.160
your laptop. A client sends you a

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:34.760
message at 9:00 p.m. asking for a status

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:36.080
update, or you're out at dinner. You

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.400
can't just pull out your MacBook at a

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:39.000
restaurant, otherwise everyone's going

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:40.560
to look at you like you have no life,

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.040
which you still might not. Or maybe

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.480
you're traveling. You're on a flight,

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:45.240
you're at a conference, you're literally

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:46.560
anywhere that isn't sitting in front of

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:48.160
your computer. Or you might be in a

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:49.960
place where there's barely any

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:51.360
connection or Wi-Fi. With all this being

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:53.200
said, Claude code is sitting on your

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:55.240
machine doing nothing. All your AI

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:56.840
agents are ready to be used aren't being

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:58.760
used at all. And God forbid an

00:00:56.840 --> 00:01:00.440
enterprise AI system goes down, and you

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:01.840
can't update it with Claude code. This

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:03.960
was a problem I've been having for years

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:05.720
now, by the way. I've got five active AI

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:07.600
apps, an agency with multiple clients,

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:09.360
and a coaching program with over 190

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:11.640
entrepreneurs. Things don't just stop

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:13.360
because I left my 3.5k month studio in

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:15.600
New York City. But now everything has

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:17.040
changed. Anthropic just dropped channels

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:18.200
for Claude code. And if you haven't

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.080
heard about this yet, let me break it

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:21.880
down real quick. A channel is basically

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:23.240
like giving Claude code a phone number.

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:25.000
It lets you talk to your Claude code

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:26.840
session through a third-party app. Right

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:29.040
now, it's been mainly just Telegram and

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:31.080
Discord, but they just added iMessage,

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:33.080
which for anyone on a Mac, this is a

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:35.680
game-changer. Think about it. You text

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:37.840
your own number from iMessage, and that

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:40.120
message gets funneled directly into your

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:41.520
running Claude code session. So, if you

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:42.920
leave your computer on, no matter where

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:44.520
you are, your Claude code can

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:46.680
continuously be working. This way you're

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:48.200
not wasting your $100 a month, $200 a

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:49.760
month subscription. Claude will even

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.240
text you back the results so you're up

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:52.840
to date with exactly what's going on

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:54.360
inside your Claude session. It's like

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:55.960
having a full-blown AI developer in your

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:58.240
pocket that has access to your entire

00:01:55.960 --> 00:02:00.840
machine without you having to be there

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:02.360
to handhold it. That's crazy. Now, let

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:03.880
me walk you through how to actually set

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:05.400
this up because it's way simpler than

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:07.320
you think. The first step, you need to

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:08.360
grant full disk access on your Mac. So,

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:10.039
you're going to open up your system

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:11.680
settings, go to privacy and security,

00:02:10.039 --> 00:02:13.200
then full [music] disk access. And

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:15.120
you're going to add whatever app you run

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:16.440
Claude code in. For me, that's VS code.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.600
If you use the actual terminal app, then

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:19.480
you can add that instead. This is

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:21.520
required because iMessage stores its

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:22.920
database locally on your Mac, and Claude

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:24.640
code needs permission to read those

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:26.240
messages. Without this step, nothing

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.680
works. Then, you want to install the

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:29.480
iMessage plugin, and this is literally

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:31.200
one command. You copy from the docs,

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:32.640
paste it into Claude code, and ask you

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.960
to confirm the install. And [music]

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:35.720
that's it. It takes it literally about

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:37.800
like 10 seconds. And by the way, if you

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:39.800
also want Telegram or Discord, those are

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:42.080
separate plugins, but the process is the

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:44.160
exact same. One command each. The next

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:45.640
step is to launch Claude code in channel

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:47.026
mode. So, instead of just running Claude

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:48.720
code normally like you've done probably

00:02:47.026 --> 00:02:50.160
[music] for every single day since 3:00

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:51.600
a.m., you paste it in a slightly

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:53.480
different launch command that tells it

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:55.120
to listen for iMessage. The second you

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:56.760
run it, you see a message that says

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:58.560
listening for channel messages from

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:00.127
iMessage. And now you're live, because

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:01.680
that means it's listening for iMessage.

00:03:00.127 --> 00:03:03.440
[music] So, to test it, you pull out

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:05.240
your phone, you open up iMessage, and

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:06.600
you text yourself something like, "Hey,

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:08.400
can you hear me?" And within a few

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:10.360
seconds, it pops up right there in your

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:12.160
Claude code terminal. Claude responds,

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:13.480
and you get to reply back on your phone.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:15.000
So, if you were timing this setup from

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:16.920
when you first started to now, this

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.840
whole setup probably took you about 5

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:20.680
minutes max. And that includes me

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:22.000
Googling what bun was because you do

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:23.560
need to install that first, which is a

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:26.240
JavaScript [music] bun. If you got any

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:27.920
issues revolving around bun, bun is a

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:29.920
JavaScript runtime that you need to

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:31.640
install first, but don't overthink it,

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:33.400
just install it. Now with your iMessage

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:35.320
and Claude code connected, let's

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:36.760
actually put it to use because there's

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:37.960
no point of having this if you're not

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:39.800
actually going to be using this for your

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:41.320
personal one-person AI business, right?

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:42.880
So, imagine you're at the gym, and you

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:44.400
want to check how your app's doing. Text

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:46.480
Claude code, "Give me a summary of

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:48.120
today's analytics for my app Deeper."

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:49.320
Boom, you get a full breakdown on your

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:50.960
phone. Or you're going to be grabbing

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:52.527
coffee, and a coaching student has a

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:54.200
question about their app architecture.

00:03:52.527 --> 00:03:55.840
[music] You text Claude code, "Review

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:58.080
this student's repo and give me the top

00:03:55.840 --> 00:04:00.080
three issues." It pulls it up, analyzes

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:01.880
it, and texts you back. Or you're on a

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:04.000
flight, and you want to prep for

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:06.360
tomorrow's client call. You can text

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:08.880
Claude code to summarize the last 10

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:10.480
commits on the client project and flag

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:11.600
anything I should know about or bring up

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:13.320
on the call. [music] And you'll get a

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:15.120
full briefing message back into your

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:16.840
iMessage. This is something you should

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:18.560
do when [music] you're having repeated

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:20.120
client calls to the same person, so that

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:22.360
way you can get a proper update on what

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:23.960
you added into the AI system that you're

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:25.440
being paid to build for them. But the

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:26.920
real benefit of all this is you're no

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:28.560
longer chained to your desk. Your Claude

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:30.960
code session has all your skills, your

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:32.600
custom agents, your analyzers, your code

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:34.800
reviews, your tools, everything. So, you

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:35.800
can access all this from your phone. And

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:37.360
for most of you, you probably have an

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:38.800
iPhone. But as good as this sounds,

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:40.760
there are some limitations you have to

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:42.360
be aware of. The biggest one, and I'm

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:44.040
sure this is intuitive, is that if your

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:45.880
Claude code session closes, like your

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:47.920
laptop dies, the channel dies. So, if

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:49.600
your laptop restarts, there's an update,

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:51.440
if you accidentally hit control C, it's

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:52.320
over. It's all gone. You have to go back

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:53.800
to your computer and start a new

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:55.400
session, which can be annoying, you

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:56.320
know, if you're gone for a few days and

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:57.760
you don't have your laptop on you

00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:58.960
because once it's closed, no one's going

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:00.880
to pick it back up. But here's a

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:03.520
workaround. You can run Claude code on a

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:05.240
Mac mini or a Mac OS VPS and keep it

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:07.080
alive with something like tmux, and now

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:08.960
it's running 24/7, and you can text it

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:10.160
whenever you want from wherever you are.

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:11.480
I'm actually in the process of setting

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:13.240
this up right now with the Mac mini that

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:14.480
just sits in my studio. So, please pray

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:16.360
for me because the last time I tried to

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:17.880
set up a server, I spent a good amount

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:19.360
of time debugging network settings.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:21.400
Luckily, one of my mentees helped me set

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:23.240
up a very good VPS, so I'm just going to

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:24.600
have him help me again. Also, you have

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:26.160
to be using Mac OS if you want to

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:27.160
connect Claude code and iMessage. I

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:29.040
mean, you can't be using Windows or

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:30.600
Linux, right? It's iMessage is an Apple

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:32.160
thing, so if you want to use this, you

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:34.600
have to have a Mac. Another big

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:35.720
misconception is this whole dispatch

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:37.400
versus [music] channels versus remote

00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:38.520
control. I want to clear something up

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:39.880
because, you know, there's three

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:41.560
different ways that you can control

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:43.320
Claude code remotely, and you might get

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:45.120
confused about which one to use. There's

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:46.480
dispatch, which is where you send a task

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:48.320
from Anthropic's mobile app, which

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:49.920
Claude runs on your machine. Uh, it's

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:50.800
best for delegating just a chunk of work

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:52.680
while you're away. Then there's

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:54.160
channels, which is what we just set up.

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:56.040
We set up the iMessage channel. There's

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:57.480
also Telegram and Discord. Then you have

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:59.000
remote control, which is best where you

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:00.040
need to actually steer what Claude is

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.520
doing. It's like you're pair

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:02.640
programming, but from your phone. They

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:04.320
all sound similar, but the key

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:06.440
difference is the trigger. Dispatch is a

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:08.280
one-off task, channels are ongoing event

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:09.720
listeners, and remote control is direct

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:11.640
steering. And honestly, for running a

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:13.400
one-person AI business, channels is the

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:15.560
one I use the most because it fits how I

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:17.440
already work. I'm texting all day anyway

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:19.000
via my iPhone, so now some of those

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:21.200
texts just happen to go to my AI

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:22.640
developer instead of my homeboy. If

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:23.680
you're running an agency, building apps,

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:25.200
doing anything [music] where you need

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:27.720
access to your dev environment on the

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:29.400
go, this is a must-have. If you want to

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:31.000
see how I built the AI apps that I'm

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:34.240
managing with this setup, [music] watch

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:34.240
this video next.

